<title>UK: BP says UK refinery unaffected by nearby fire.</title>
<headline>BP says UK refinery unaffected by nearby fire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum said its 200,000 barrel per day Grangemouth, Scotland refinery was unaffected by a fire at a nearby chemicals plant on Monday, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It appears there was an incident at Ross Chemicals, but there was certainly no affect on BP. It was not on our site,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>A police spokesman at nearby Stirling said the fire at a tank at Ross Chemicals and Storage was now under control.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
